From afa6d9d2859a907a1060de0ebee4da437f201903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:19:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ui): cache the shown operation status on a world write
 revision

The tree, the status bar, the operation page and the debug panel computed
operation::status_of (the full generation stamp) for each operation on
each frame. They now read operation::status_shown / stale_reason_shown.
These keep the answer for each operation until the world write revision
moves.

- schema::WorldRevision and app::world_rev: one flecs observer on the
  wildcard id and one on the wildcard pair. Each OnAdd, OnSet and
  OnRemove of each component (except the read-time memos GeoSig and
  GeomPrintMemo) takes a fresh number from one process counter.
- SetSetupPostScriptOptions wrote SetupDef in place (no OnSet event).
  It now clones and sets.
- Generation, verify, collision checks, the post, the post dialog, MCP
  and the script API keep calling status_of, the uncached truth.
- Row 7: op_page, state and shell read the toolpath through
  model::with_toolpath and do not clone it.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/status_cache.rs (a build count, one test for
each writer, undo and redo, project load, and a source scan that refuses
an in-place component write) and by frame_cost_ops_probe (no status is
computed on a still frame with 1 and 8 operations).

Refs #2201

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
